  "vo_pace_words_per_min": 204.5,
  "transcript": "The 2030s will be the start of a new renaissance. Let's start! What can I explain? We all know AI is changing everything. New stations say we live in unprecedented times. What they don't realise is all of this has happened before. Do you plan to take over the world? The year is 1440 and this guy invents the printing press. A machine that brought knowledge, stories and scientific advancements to a scale the world had never seen before. Within a hundred years, 30,000 books turned into 200 million printed and spread across Europe. But that actually became a huge problem. Because once everyone was given the power to say anything, finding information wasn't difficult. Finding something meaningful was. Until eventually, this guy decided it was time for the rebirth of a lost human spirit. Or as the French say, as a renaissance. Where real art and knowledge became more important than endless tablets. But now our ways of communication are changing. Again, most companies believe the next rebirth of media belongs to those who pump out the most content the fastest. But we believe they're making the same mistake people made 500 years ago. Because the reason you treasure that handmade gift or cry at your favourite movie isn't because a machine pumped it out in a second. It's because they're made by real people putting in hours of effort, making things the scrappy and half-heart ways. Hilling stories that come from an honest human voice. We believe the next generation of brands won't win by just making more, they'll win by making things people actually care about. So, if this is the next renaissance, what part will you go?",
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 2.8,
      "text": "The 2030s will be the start of a new renaissance."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.6,
      "end": 4.12,
      "text": "Let's start!"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.54,
      "end": 5.16,
      "text": "What can I explain?"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.38,
      "end": 6.84,
      "text": "We all know AI is changing everything."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.06,
      "end": 9.68,
      "text": "New stations say we live in unprecedented times."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.82,
      "end": 12.82,
      "text": "What they don't realise is all of this has happened before."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.0,
      "end": 15.14,
      "text": "Do you plan to take over the world?"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.84,
      "end": 19.36,
      "text": "The year is 1440 and this guy invents the printing press."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.76,
      "end": 25.26,
      "text": "A machine that brought knowledge, stories and scientific advancements to a scale the world had never seen before."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.26,
      "end": 31.08,
      "text": "Within a hundred years, 30,000 books turned into 200 million printed and spread across Europe."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.2,
      "end": 33.1,
      "text": "But that actually became a huge problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.26,
      "end": 37.38,
      "text": "Because once everyone was given the power to say anything, finding information wasn't difficult."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.74,
      "end": 39.56,
      "text": "Finding something meaningful was."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.88,
      "end": 44.64,
      "text": "Until eventually, this guy decided it was time for the rebirth of a lost human spirit."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.8,
      "end": 47.56,
      "text": "Or as the French say, as a renaissance."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.2,
      "end": 51.92,
      "text": "Where real art and knowledge became more important than endless tablets."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.32,
      "end": 54.46,
      "text": "But now our ways of communication are changing."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.0,
      "end": 61.08,
      "text": "Again, most companies believe the next rebirth of media belongs to those who pump out the most content the fastest."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.48,
      "end": 65.24,
      "text": "But we believe they're making the same mistake people made 500 years ago."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.3,
      "end": 71.52,
      "text": "Because the reason you treasure that handmade gift or cry at your favourite movie isn't because a machine pumped it out in a second."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.74,
      "end": 76.9,
      "text": "It's because they're made by real people putting in hours of effort, making things the scrappy and half-heart ways."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.14,
      "end": 79.6,
      "text": "Hilling stories that come from an honest human voice."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.6,
      "end": 86.1,
      "text": "We believe the next generation of brands won't win by just making more, they'll win by making things people actually care about."
    },
    {
      "start": 86.32,
      "end": 89.96,
      "text": "So, if this is the next renaissance, what part will you go?"
    }
  ],
